# TypeScript Monorepo Tooling

Use this rule when changing workspace tooling, TypeScript config, or root
scripts.

## Core Pattern

- Keep root `typecheck` no-emit. Use `tsconfig.typecheck.json` for the
  source graph and exclude generated `dist`.
- Keep package `build` scripts responsible for emit and package `typecheck`
  scripts responsible for `--noEmit`.
- Keep package `"types"` entries pointed at `dist/index.d.ts`; do not point
  published-facing metadata at `src`.
- Add root dev dependencies for scripts under `scripts/` when root
  typechecking needs to resolve them.
- Keep `pnpm precommit` as the full CI-parity routine and
  `pnpm precommit:fast` as the Docker-free local loop.
- Keep Lefthook config in `lefthook.yml`: pre-commit runs the fast routine,
  pre-push runs the Docker-backed full routine.

## Integration Points

- `package.json` owns root verification commands.
- `tsconfig.typecheck.json` checks `apps`, `packages`, and `scripts`.
- `scripts/precommit.ts` owns local precommit orchestration.
- `lefthook.yml` owns actual Git hook wiring.
- Package `tsconfig.json` files exclude `**/*.test.ts` from emit.
- `.github/workflows/ci.yml` must use `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`.

## Common Pitfalls

| Pitfall | Preferred handling |
| --- | --- |
| Running `pnpm build` inside `typecheck` | Use no-emit typechecking only |
| Pointing package `types` to `src/index.ts` | Keep `types` on `dist/index.d.ts` |
| Letting root globs include generated declarations | Exclude `**/dist/**` |
| Loosening CI lockfile installs | Keep frozen lockfile installs |

